Macintosh NetHack 3.0j pl10 has been rebuilt, repackaged and
redistributed (i.e. now on linc.cis.upenn.edu [130.91.6.8] in
pub/NH3.0/mac).

The vast majority of mac hackers were able to use the previous
pl10 distribution.  Isolated users (most notably mac IIfx'ers
and system 7.0 eager beavers) had problems with the previous
distribution.  Those users should find that the game in
nh30j+.hqx solves their problems with Mac NetHack if they can
afford a 3M MultiFinder partition (less, iff you keep an eye
on memory use).

One other area of concern is that Mac NetHack should only be
played on the main screen (else the results are unpredictable).

As always, messages should be directed to:
nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu

Enjoy! ...

